@startuml environment-context
' Editable source for the Environment context and information-flow boundary.
' Sources: ../SRS.tex G.6, G.8 and S.2 (FR-FLT, FR-UI, FR-REV, FR-AI).
' Draft reference: C:/Users/itari/Documents/SRS.tex E.2--E.5.
' Render: java -jar plantuml.jar -tpdf environment-context.puml
' Preview: java -jar plantuml.jar -tsvg environment-context.puml
!pragma layout smetana
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam wrapWidth 210
title FPVR external context

actor "User" as User
rectangle "Physical activity space" as Space
rectangle "Input options overall\nQuest motion controllers OR\ncompatible Xbox controller" as Input
rectangle "Quest headset and XR runtime" as XR
rectangle "PCVR host and headset link\n(PCVR mode only)" as Host
rectangle "FPVR system boundary\nFlight simulation; courses and recovery;\nperformance evaluation; VR interaction" as FPVR
rectangle "Optional analysis dependency\nLocation and interface undecided" as AI

Space --> User : physical surroundings and clearance
User --> Space : prepares stationary activity area
User --> Input : flight axes and button actions
Input --> FPVR : control values and device availability
User --> FPVR : mode, level and recovery choices
FPVR --> User : instructions, flight view and current results
XR --> FPVR : pose/input availability and runtime status
FPVR --> XR : rendered imagery and runtime interaction
Host ..> FPVR : conditional host/link resources and availability
FPVR ..> Host : conditional PC-executed application presentation
FPVR ..> AI : conditional analysis inputs; payload unapproved
AI ..> FPVR : conditional feedback or unavailable/error outcome

note bottom of Space
  Physical clearance is prepared by the user or guardian.
  No direct FPVR sensor feed or obstacle detection is assumed.
end note
note bottom of Input
  Both controller types are required overall.
  Exact models and per-mode combinations remain under review.
end note
note bottom of AI
  Intelligent feedback is conditional; standard review remains available.
  An external service is only a possibility. No provider, network protocol,
  transmitted payload or privacy decision is approved by this diagram.
end note

legend bottom
  Solid arrow: baseline interaction; label names information or influence.
  Dashed arrow: conditional dependency, not a mandatory connection.
  Arrowheads indicate direction; arrows do not prescribe physical wiring.
  No physical drone is connected to FPVR.
endlegend
@enduml
